[Music]  agents it has been seven days since your  activation after the president invoked  national security presidential directive  51 and 19 days since this pandemic was  first recognized  if you are receiving this message you  have managed to negate the growing  violence and meet up with the other  members of your cell  in your designated safe house you'll  have noticed a number of shd gadgets  that you can utilize in your mission  but recently our friends on the research  and development team have gone one step  further  while the mobile communications network  is down across the country using the  division network they've managed to  bring us back online using your personal  device in something they call  resurgence  [Music]  resurgence is ubisoft's first mobile  entry into the division universe  but this isn't just a port of the  division one or two this is a fully  standalone game based within the same  universe as the base games  keeping true to its roots resurgence  will be an open world cover shooter a  looter shooter rpg and will contain both  pve and pvp elements  in essence this is the game we've been  playing for the last six years but with  a new story and available on your mobile  phone  the seating places the player as a first  wave agent who was activated in the  early days of the pandemic during the  events of the division one where a  devastating pandemic sweeps through new  york city on black friday and one by one  basic services begin to fail  within weeks society collapses into  chaos and the government activates the  division a classified unit of sleeper  agents  leading seemingly ordinary lives among  us division agents are trained to  operate independently of command when  all other means have failed  the division resurgence story is  completely canon running alongside the  timeline of existing events spanning all  the way through to the division two  this new addition to the story will  cater to both new and existing fans of  the franchise it is a standalone game  where no previous experience is required  we will see some familiar faces included  such as the rioters cleaners my personal  favorite rikers black tusk and a new  hostile faction called freeman  resurgence has both pve and pvp  activities  the large open world map has players  placed at the heart of manhattan new  york and there are campaign missions  dotted throughout that can be run solo  or co-op  here is a short clip of one of the  earlier missions where the player is  helping agent kelly fight through a  group of enemies in order to secure some  medical supplies  on target  clear  shot agent  clear  here's an elevator  look speed up  hope it works  i don't like that sound  cover me while i fix this  going down  not again cover me  here we go  god  keep them down  there enough mishaps  we should have been activated a week ago  i don't know why while they waited  stupid or incompetent  but i guess we get the leaders we  deserve right  guess you're wondering  maybe it's the system that's messed up  [Music]  trinity church isn't far let's move  however if you decide you'd rather  explore there are a number of open world  activities to stumble across which will  only take you around five minutes to  complete  in the division resurgence all campaign  missions side missions and open world  activities will be playable solo as well  as co-op  pvp which includes the dark zone and  other modes will be available at launch  but won't be present during the closed  alpha  the division resurgence is following its  routes by ensuring that deep rpg  elements will stay intact  there will be looting modding of weapons  crafting of items and other gear and of  course the ability to upgrade  as per all good luda shooters  it's about being able to build and grow  your character which best suits your  style of play  crafting works in a similar way to the  division 1 and 2 where players can  exchange looted materials for weapons  and gear  however it's not quite as  straightforward as that  for example each class of weapon has its  own crafting tree where new blueprints  can be unlocked  leveling up your crafting experience  will also increase your chances of  higher quality equipment being produced  with better base stats  mods offer similar bonuses to the other  games but with the additions of  attributes like toughness weapon damage  and a number of different types of skill  damage  this will mean that making the right  choice between mods will be more  important having a greater impact on  builds  with this in mind there is also another  layer to this where players can choose  between a number of different classes  they start out with each with their own  unique skills gadgets and signature  ultimate skill  each class also has a unique talent tree  which when upgraded can alter the  effectiveness of the gadgets and skills  available  while you're only able to choose one of  these to start with over time players  will be able to unlock others and there  are more to be released in future  seasons  being a mobile game the controls for  this sort of genre are a bit of a  talking point  however this seems to work quite nicely  when properly utilizing the in-game  cover system this could be manual or  automatic leaving it up to the player to  find the best configuration as well as  fully customizable control layout in  settings  the division resurgence is a  free-to-play mobile game  naturally this is a scary term for a lot  of gamers to hear as this often raises  the question so what are the micro  transactions going to be like  much like we've seen in the division 1  and 2 this doesn't mean we'll be seeing  pay to win elements being added nothing  will be locked behind paywalls and  everything that can be purchased will be  accessible and unlockable for free  purchasing options will only enable the  player to progress faster or unlock  certain cosmetics  however content called seasons will  continue to be pushed out every three to  four months with other events like  cosmetics and gameplay being released in  between  each season will contain a new main  mission a new class and manhunt as well  as a new battle pass exotic weapon  cosmetics game modes and even expansions  on the open world area  it really must be stated that everything  i've talked about here and have shown in  the video is being developed completely  separate from the studio working on the  division two they're continuing to work  on bringing new content to the game with  a lot more planned for the coming months  apart from the overarching story the  teams working on resurgence are from a  number of different studios that are  experts in mobile games doing their best  to bring tom clancy's the division to  handheld devices  using the unreal engine the intention is  to bring the aaa experience to mobile  this will be available on most high-end  phones but is still being optimized as  we speak to include as many devices as  possible  this is definitely an ambitious  undertaking i'm not a mobile gamer by  any means but the detail and sheer size  of the open world has had me pretty  excited about this addition to the  franchise for a while now  there has been a lot of focus on keeping  the transitions through the open world  as seamless as possible and this is  showing  my software development skills don't  overlap into the gaming industry all  that much but i can only imagine the  challenges around creating a game as  detailed as the division on mobile while  still making it playable to the majority  of users without needing a phone that's  less than a couple of months old  the addition of story elements that are  in the same universe as the original  games only furthers my excitement  what more will we see from before the  events of the division one regarding the  first wave  will there be story crossovers  or more importantly will my giant hands  and sausage fingers be able to play this  on a phone or should i just 